 by day. Music after dark.With your mates → cite24†Image: Two visitors relaxing together at an outdoor festival event SOMETHING TO LOOK FORWARD TO A WEEKEND\nL68: FOR TWO Even if only one of you lives for bikes.Coming together → cite25†Image: Two motorcyclists giving a thumbs up on a woodland trail FOLLOW YOUR CURIOSITY HERE FOR\nL69: THE RIDING?New bikes. New skills. Your next adventure.Explore riding →\nL70: First ABR? You’re in good company. [Button: Start with our first-timer guide →]\nL71: \nL72: IT’S THE WHOLE WEEKEND\nL73: ## FROM MORNING\nL74: TO NIGHT\nL75: \nL76: Here’s one way to spend a day at ABR. Make it your own.\nL77: \nL78:   1. 01\nL79: \nL80: MORNING\nL81: \nL82: cite26†Image: A motorcyclist exploring a woodland trail at ABR Festival L83: \nL84: ### COFFEE,\nL85: THEN ADVENTURE\nL86: \nL87: Start with a free morning brew from the on-site Mitas PitStops, then try a bike you’ve had your eye on, build your riding skills, or head out on the trails.\nL88: \nL89: cite2†Find your kind of riding → L90: \nL91:   2. 02\nL92: \nL93: AFTERNOON\nL94: \nL95: cite27†Image: A motorcycle demonstration with visitors watching under a festival tent L96: ### BROWSE. WATCH.\nL97: CATCH UP.\nL98: \nL99: Grab a bite to eat from your choice of over 60 vendors, catch a talk from the biggest names in motorcycling, and explore over 200 exhibitors. Leave time for the conversations you hadn’t planned.\nL100: \nL101: cite0†Explore what's on → L102: \nL103:   3. 03\nL104: \nL105: AFTER DARK\nL106: \nL107: cite28†Image: Live music on the Bikerheadz Stage at ABR Festival L108: ### PARK THE BIKE,\nL109: STAY FOR THE NIGHT\nL110: \nL111: Meet up with your mates, find a band in one of the six music venues, and settle into the evening. One more song, one more story. Your tent will be waiting when you’re ready.\nL112: \nL113: cite1†Explore after dark → L114: \nL115: A flavour of your weekend. Look out for the 2027 programme announcements.\nL116: \nL117: > “As always, had a fantastic time with my mates and made new friends along the way with plans to all meet up again.”2026 visitor survey · returning attendee\nL118: cite29†Image: Aerial view of Ragley Hall and the ABR Festival campsite L119: \nL120: MAKE YOURSELF AT HOME\nL121: ## PITCH UP\nL122: AND SETTLE IN\nL123: \nL124: Bring your tent and stay for the weekend. Friday and Saturday night camping, toilets and hot showers are included in your weekend ticket.\nL125: \nL126: Prefer a tent ready when you arrive? Take a look at the accommodation upgrades.\nL127: \nL128: cite7†Explore pre-pitched tents → L129: \nL130: cite8†Explore glamping →†www.tickettailor.com cite11†Camping & arrival information → cite12†Accessibility → L131: \nL132: MORE WEEKEND FOR YOUR MONEY\nL133: ## A BIG WEEKEND\nL134: AT SENSIBLE PRICES\nL135: \nL136: Your ticket gets you much more than entry. Set up camp, catch a talk, try a bike and head to the music. So much of the weekend is already covered.\nL137: \nL138: A PINT FOR UNDER £4\nL139: \nL140: A MEAL FOR£10\nL141: \nL142: Food and drink are paid for separately, with options at these prices.\nL143: ### WHAT'S INCLUDED IN YOUR WEEKEND TICKET?\nL144: \nL145:   * Two nights under the stars Friday and Saturday camping, posh toilets and hot showers.\nL146:   * Your days, filled Over 80 guest speaker sessions, 200+ exhibitors, manufacturer test rides, off-road tuition and guided rides.\nL147:   * Your nights, sorted Live music across six venues and a whole festival to enjoy with your mates.\nL148: \nL149: Own-bike trail passes, Super Thursday, accommodation upgrades and applicable vehicle supplements cost extra.\nL150: \nL151: cite30†See your Early Bird ticket → L152: GET NEXT SUMMER IN THE DIARY\nL153: ## YOUR SUMMER HOLIDAY\nL154: IS\nL155: SORTED\nL156: \nL157: 25–27 June 2027\nL158: Ragley Hall, Warwickshire\nL159: \nL160: Want an extra day?\nL161: cite13†Add Super Thursday, 24 June, for £89 → Separate add-on · requires a weekend ticket\nL162: \nL163: EARLY BIRD WEEKEND\nL164: \nL165: £169 Save £50 against the £219 full-price ticket\nL166: ### A LOT OF WEEKEND IN ONE TICKET\nL167: \nL168:   * Three days of festival admission\nL169:   * Live music across six venues, over 80 guest speaker sessions, 200+ exhibitors, 60+ food stalls, 20+ bars, and more\nL170:   * Two nights of camping, posh toilets as standard, and hot showers\nL171:   * Manufacturer test rides, off-road tuition, and guided rides, all included with your ticket\nL172: A quick word on extras. Own-bike trail access, Thursday, accommodation upgrades and applicable vehicle supplements cost extra. Food, drink and purchases are separate.\nL173: \nL174: cite18†Get Early Bird tickets → cite15†Day tickets & other options → L175: \nL176: LET’S MAKE IT EASY\nL177: ## FIRST TIME?\nL178: START HERE.\nL179: \nL180: From choosing your ticket to finding your camping spot, here are the things worth knowing before you arrive.\nL181: \nL182: Your first ABR: the practical guide →\nL183: \nL184: Do I have to ride off road?\nL185: Not at all. Riding the trails is only one part of a jam-packed itinerary of things to do at the ABR Festival. You can spend your time enjoying music, talks, test rides, the exhibitor village, photo festival, food festival, kayaking, axe throwing, the festival atmosphere, and so much more without a trail pass.\nL186: \nL187: When do I need a trail pass?\nL188: A Trail Pass is needed to ride your own bike on the on-site trails. You do not need a trail pass if you want to take part in off-road tuition, test rides, or green lane rideouts. cite4†Explore the trails. L189: \nL190: How do I arrange test rides?\nL191: \nL192: All bookings are done on the day at each manufacturer’s stand. Slots and licence requirements vary, so make sure you check with them before you queue up. cite3†Read the test-ride information. L193: \nL194: Can we camp together if we arrive separately?\nL195: Plan to arrive together if you want to camp together: camping spaces are not reserved for groups. cite11†Visitor FAQs. L196: \nL197: cite11†All festival FAQs → L198: \nL199: cite17†Image: ABR Festival visitors cheering and enjoying the event L200: ## SEE YOU\nL201: AT RAGLEY.\nL202: \nL203: 25–27 June 2027 · Early Bird weekend £169\nL204: \nL205: cite18†Let’s make a weekend of it → L206: \nL207: [Button: ✕]\nL208: \nL209: The good people backing us in 2027\nL210: \nL211: cite31†Image: Alpinestars L212: \nL213: cite32†Image: Bikerheadz L214: \nL215: cite33†Image: Bridgestone L216: \nL217: cite34†Image: Cardo L218: \nL219: cite35†Image: Ducati L220: \nL221: cite36†Image: Dunlop L222: \nL223: cite37†Image: Five Advanced Gloves L224: \nL225: cite38†Image: GoPro L226: \nL227: cite39†Image: Halvarssons L228: \nL229: cite40†Image: Helly Hansen L230: \nL231: cite41†Image: Honda L232: \nL233: cite42†Image: In&Motion L234: \nL235: cite43†Image: JUSTRIDE L236: \nL237: cite44†Image: McAMS L238: \nL239: cite45†Image: Michelin L240: \nL241: cite46†Image: Mitas L242: cite47†Image: Muc-Off L243: \nL244: cite48†Image: Öhlins L245: \nL246: cite49†Image: Phoenix PROskills TRAILS L247: \nL248: cite50†Image: REV'IT! L249: \nL250: cite51†Image: Royal Enfield L251: \nL252: cite52†Image: Rukka L253: \nL254: cite53†Image: Schuberth L255: \nL256: cite54†Image: Scorpion L257: \nL258: cite55†Image: Spada L259: \nL260: cite56†Image: Spada L261: \nL262: cite57†Image: ZERO Motorcycles L263: \nL264:   * cite58†Gallery†gallery.abrfestival.com L265:   * cite59†About L266:   * cite14†News L267:   * cite11†FAQs L268:   * cite60†Contact Us L269:   * cite12†Accessibility L270:   * cite61†Privacy Policy L271: \nL272: cite62†Image: abrfestival2027-footer L273: \nL274: GET THE LATEST ABR FESTIVAL NEWS DIRECT TO YOUR INBOX\nL275: cite63†Image: ABR Festival was awarded Consumer Event of the Year at the PPA Awards in 2024 and 2025 L